d's largest displacement crisis → Chad, Egypt, Ethiopia destabilized\n- 🇮🇷 **Iran-Israel 2025/26** → Strait of Hormuz risk → global oil price shock\n- 🇵🇰 **Pakistan-Afghanistan 2026** → South Asia security crisis → regional trade disruption\n\n## Why it matters\n\n| Who benefits | How |\n|---|---|\n| Governments | Predict economic shocks before they hit |\n| Journalists | Explain global consequences with real data |\n| NGOs | Decide where to send aid before the crisis peaks |\n| Regular people | Understand why their grocery bill went up |\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Why Gemma 3 (4B Instruction-Tuned)?\n\n**Model:** `gemma-3-4b-it`\n**Framework:** Transformers (Hugging Face) + PyTorch\n\n**Why this model:**\n- `4b` = 4 billion parameters — smart enough for deep analysis,\n   small enough to run on Kaggle's free GPU without crashing\n- `it` = instruction-tuned — I can ask it plain English questions\n   like *\"what economic effects did this war cause?\"* and it answers clearly\n- Transformers library loads it in 5 lines of code — beginner-friendly\n   but research-grade powerful\n\n**In simple terms:** It's the right balance of brain size and speed\nfor a research notebook running on free cloud hardware.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"---\n## 1 - Setup & Installation\n\n### Why Gemma 3 (4B Instruction-Tuned)?\n\n- `4b` = 4 billion parameters — smart enough for deep analysis, small enough to run on Kaggle's **free T4 GPU** without crashing\n- `it` = instruction-tuned — we can ask it plain English questions like *\"what economic effects did this war cause?\"* and it answers clearly\n- **Transformers** library loads it in 5 lines of code — beginner-friendly but research-grade powerful\n\nIn simple terms: it's the right balance of **brain size and speed** for a research notebook on free cloud hardware.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Install any missing libraries\n# Kaggle already has most of these; this cell makes sure everything is ready\n!pip install -q transformers accelerate bitsandbytes sentencepiece\n\n# Core data libraries\nimport numpy as np          # math and number crunching\nimport pandas as pd         # tables and data manipulation\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt   # basic charts\nimport matplotlib.patches as mpatches\nimport seaborn as sns       # prettier charts\nimport warnings\nwarnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n\n# AI / model libraries\nimport torch                # the engine that runs the AI math\nfrom transformers import AutoTokenizer, AutoModelForCausalLM\n\n# Check if GPU is available\ndevice = 'cuda' if torch.cuda.is_available() else 'cpu'\nprint(f\"Device: {device.upper()}\")\nif device == 'cuda':\n    gpu_name = torch.cuda.get_device_name(0)\n    gpu_mem  = torch.cuda.get_device_properties(0).total_memory / 1e9\n    print(f\"   GPU  : {gpu_name}\")\n    print(f\"   VRAM : {gpu_mem:.1f} GB\")\nelse:\n    print(\"    No GPU found — model loading will be slow\")\n\n# Chart style\nplt.rcParams['figure.facecolor'] = '#0d1117'   # dark background\nplt.rcParams['axes.facecolor']   = '#161b22'\nplt.rcParams['text.color']       = 'white'\nplt.rcParams['axes.labelcolor']  = 'white'\nplt.rcParams['xtick.color']      = 'white'\nplt.rcParams['ytick.color']      = 'white'\nplt.rcParams['axes.edgecolor']   = '#30363d'\nplt.rcParams['grid.color']       = '#21262d'\nplt.rcParams['font.family']      = 'DejaVu Sans'\n\nprint(\"\\n All libraries loaded. Ready to begin.\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-03-20T19:19:54.202546Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-03-20T19:19:54.203115Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-03-20T19:19:58.507236Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-03-20T19:19:54.203082Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-03-20T19:19:58.505968Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Device: CPU\n    No GPU found — model loading will be slow\n\n All libraries loaded. Ready to begin.\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":15},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**What this cell does:**  \nInstalls any missing Python packages, then loads all the tools we need — data tools (Pandas, NumPy), chart tools (Matplotlib, Seaborn), and AI tools (Transformers, PyTorch).  \n\n**Why:** Think of this as setting up your kitchen before cooking. You need the right tools on the counter before you start. We also check whether a GPU is available — the GPU is like having an industrial oven instead of a home microwave. It processes AI calculations much faster.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"---\n## 2 - Data Loading\n\nWe load **two types of data**:\n1. **Conflict data** — when wars started, where, and how intense they were\n2. **Economic indicator data** — oil prices, inflation, food price index, refugee counts over time\n\nThe conflict dataset covers **2003–2026**, including all currently active major conflicts as of March 2026.  \nData sourced from: ACLED, UCDP, UN OCHA, World Bank, IMF, UNHCR, African Development Bank.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# DATASET 1 — Major Active Conflicts (2003–2026)\n# Sources: ACLED, UCDP, UN OCHA, World Bank, IMF, UNHCR\n# Updated: March 2026 — includes all currently active major conflicts\n\nconflicts = pd.DataFrame({\n    'conflict': [\n        'Iraq War',\n        'Syria Civil War',\n        'Libya Civil War',\n        'Yemen War',\n        'Myanmar Civil War',\n        'Ukraine War',\n        'Sudan Civil War',\n        'Gaza Conflict',\n        'Iran-Israel War',           # 2026 — ceasefire Jun 2025, flare-ups ongoing\n        'Pakistan-Afghanistan War',  # 2026 — Pakistan struck Afghanistan Feb 27 2026\n        'Lebanon War (2026)',        # 2026 — ceasefire collapsed Mar 2, 2026\n    ],\n    'country': [\n        'Iraq', 'Syria', 'Libya', 'Yemen',\n        'Myanmar', 'Ukraine', 'Sudan', 'Gaza/Palestine',\n        'Iran/Israel', 'Pakistan/Afghanistan', 'Lebanon'\n    ],\n    'start_year': [\n        2003, 2011, 2011, 2015,\n        2021, 2022, 2023, 2023,\n        2025, 2026, 2026\n    ],\n    # Current status as of March 2026\n    'status_2026': [\n        'Legacy / Low intensity',\n        'Transitional govt (post-Assad)',\n        'Fragmented / Low intensity',\n        'Active',\n        'Active — junta losing ground',\n        'Active — frontlines largely frozen',\n        'Active — world largest displacement crisis',\n        'Active — fragile ceasefire',\n        'Ceasefire (Jun 2025) — fragile',\n        'Active (Feb 27, 2026)',\n        'Active — resumed Mar 2, 2026',\n    ],\n    'region': [\n        'Middle East', 'Middle East', 'North Africa', 'Middle East',\n        'Southeast Asia', 'Europe', 'Africa', 'Middle East',\n        'Middle East', 'South Asia', 'Middle East'\n    ],\n    'intensity': [\n        'Low', 'Medium', 'Medium', 'High',\n        'Very High', 'Very High', 'Very High', 'Very High',\n        'High', 'High', 'High'\n    ],\n    # People displaced in millions — UNHCR / IOM / UN OCHA\n    'displaced_M': [\n        4.2,   # Iraq — UNHCR historical figure\n        13.5,  # Syria — largest protracted refugee crisis globally\n        1.3,   # Libya\n        4.5,   # Yemen\n        3.0,   # Myanmar — 3M+ IDPs (UN 2025); 80,000+ fled to India/Thailand/Bangladesh\n        8.2,   # Ukraine — 8M+ refugees to Europe (UNHCR)\n        12.0,  # Sudan — world's LARGEST active displacement crisis (IOM Jul 2025)\n        1.9,   # Gaza\n        0.4,   # Iran-Israel — estimated internal displacement from strikes\n        0.3,   # Pakistan-Afghanistan — early estimates, Feb 2026 conflict\n        0.5,   # Lebanon — conflict resumed Mar 2, 2026 after ceasefire collapse\n    ],\n    # GDP contraction % in the conflict country — IMF / World Bank / African Dev Bank\n    'gdp_shock_pct': [\n        -8.5,   # Iraq\n        -22.4,  # Syria\n        -11.2,  # Libya\n        -30.1,  # Yemen\n        -18.0,  # Myanmar — 18% GDP drop in 2021 (UNDP/CNN); still 12% below pre-coup\n        -29.1,  # Ukraine\n        -37.5,  # Sudan — GDP contracted 37.5% in 2023 (African Development Bank)\n        -40.5,  # Gaza\n        -5.0,   # Iran — sanctions tightened + strike damage (estimated)\n        -3.5,   # Pakistan — economic strain from conflict + sanctions risk (estimated)\n        -8.0,   # Lebanon — conflict restart layered on existing economic collapse (estimated)\n    ],\n    # Countries significantly affected by ripple effects (energy, food, migration, politics)\n    'neighbors_affected': [\n        5,   # Iraq → Iran, Kuwait, Syria, Jordan, Turkey\n        6,   # Syria → Turkey, Lebanon, Jordan, Iraq, Europe, Egypt\n        4,   # Libya → Tunisia, Chad, Egypt, Italy (migration)\n        4,   # Yemen → Saudi Arabia, Oman, Egypt, global shipping\n        5,   # Myanmar → Thailand, India, Bangladesh, China, Laos\n        8,   # Ukraine → all of Europe (energy), Middle East (wheat), Global\n        6,   # Sudan → Chad, Egypt, South Sudan, Ethiopia, CAR, Libya\n        5,   # Gaza → Egypt, Jordan, Lebanon, Red Sea global shipping\n        7,   # Iran-Israel → Gulf states, oil markets, US bases, Strait of Hormuz\n        4,   # Pakistan-Afghanistan → India, Iran, Central Asia, China\n        4,   # Lebanon → Israel, Syria, Cyprus, Mediterranean trade routes\n    ]\n})\n\n# ── Severity score: how much ripple does each conflict send globally? ──\n# Formula: (displaced people × neighbors affected) / abs(GDP shock)\n# Higher score = bigger butterfly effect on the rest of the world\nconflicts['severity_score'] = (\n    conflicts['displaced_M'] * conflicts['neighbors_affected']\n    / conflicts['gdp_shock_pct'].abs()\n).round(2)\n\nprint(\"── Conflict Dataset (Updated to March 2026) ──────────\")\nprint(f\"Total conflicts tracked : {conflicts.shape[0]}\")\nprint(f\"Features per conflict   : {conflicts.shape[1]}\")\nactive = conflicts[conflicts['status_2026'].str.startswith('Active')]\nprint(f\"Currently active (2026) : {len(active)} conflicts\")\nprint(f\"Total people displaced  : {conflicts['displaced_M'].sum():.1f} million\")\nprint()\nconflicts[['conflict', 'start_year', 'status_2026',\n           'displaced_M', 'gdp_shock_pct',\n           'neighbors_affected', 'severity_score']]","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-03-20T19:19:58.509212Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-03-20T19:19:58.509671Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-03-20T19:19:58.548028Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-03-20T19:19:58.509627Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-03-20T19:19:58.546705Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"── Conflict Dataset (Updated to March 2026) ──────────\nTotal conflicts tracked : 11\nFeatures per conflict   : 10\nCurrently active (2026) : 7 conflicts\nTotal people displaced  : 49.8 million\n\n","output_type":"stream"},{"execution_count":16,"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":"                    conflict  start_year  \\\n0                   Iraq War        2003   \n1            Syria Civil War        2011   \n2            Libya Civil War        2011   \n3                  Yemen War        2015   \n4          Myanmar Civil War        2021   \n5                Ukraine War        2022   \n6            Sudan Civil War        2023   \n7              Gaza Conflict        2023   \n8            Iran-Israel War        2025   \n9   Pakistan-Afghanistan War        2026   \n10        Lebanon War (2026)        2026   \n\n                                   status_2026  displaced_M  gdp_shock_pct  \\\n0                       Legacy / Low intensity          4.2           -8.5   \n1               Transitional govt (post-Assad)         13.5          -22.4   \n2                   Fragmented / Low intensity          1.3          -11.2   \n3                                       Active          4.5          -30.1   \n4                 Active — junta losing ground          3.0          -18.0   \n5           Active — frontlines largely frozen          8.2          -29.1   \n6   Active — world largest displacement crisis         12.0          -37.5   \n7                   Active — fragile ceasefire          1.9          -40.5   \n8               Ceasefire (Jun 2025) — fragile          0.4           -5.0   \n9                        Active (Feb 27, 2026)          0.3           -3.5   \n10                Active — resumed Mar 2, 2026          0.5           -8.0   \n\n    neighbors_affected  severity_score  \n0                    5            2.47  \n1                    6            3.62  \n2                    4            0.46  \n3                    4            0.60  \n4                    5            0.83  \n5                    8            2.25  \n6                    6            1.92  \n7                    5            0.23  \n8                    7            0.56  \n9                    4            0.34  \n10                   4            0.25  ","text/html":"<div>\n<style scoped>\n    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n        vertical-align: middle;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n        vertical-align: top;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe thead th {\n        text-align: right;\n    }\n</style>\n<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n      <th></th>\n      <th>conflict</th>\n      <th>start_year</th>\n      <th>status_2026</th>\n      <th>displaced_M</th>\n      <th>gdp_shock_pct</th>\n      <th>neighbors_affected</th>\n      <th>severity_score</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <th>0</th>\n      <td>Iraq War</td>\n      <td>2003</td>\n      <td>Legacy / Low intensity</td>\n      <td>4.2</td>\n      <td>-8.5</td>\n      <td>5</td>\n      <td>2.47</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>1</th>\n      <td>Syria Civil War</td>\n      <td>2011</td>\n      <td>Transitional govt (post-Assad)</td>\n      <td>13.5</td>\n      <td>-22.4</td>\n      <td>6</td>\n      <td>3.62</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>2</th>\n      <td>Libya Civil War</td>\n      <td>2011</td>\n      <td>Fragmented / Low intensity</td>\n      <td>1.3</td>\n      <td>-11.2</td>\n      <td>4</td>\n      <td>0.46</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>3</th>\n      <td>Yemen War</td>\n      <td>2015</td>\n      <td>Active</td>\n      <td>4.5</td>\n      <td>-30.1</td>\n      <td>4</td>\n      <td>0.60</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>4</th>\n      <td>Myanmar Civil War</td>\n      <td>2021</td>\n      <td>Active — junta losing ground</td>\n      <td>3.0</td>\n      <td>-18.0</td>\n      <td>5</td>\n      <td>0.83</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>5</th>\n      <td>Ukraine War</td>\n      <td>2022</td>\n      <td>Active — frontlines largely frozen</td>\n      <td>8.2</td>\n      <td>-29.1</td>\n      <td>8</td>\n      <td>2.25</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>6</th>\n      <td>Sudan Civil War</td>\n      <td>2023</td>\n      <td>Active — world largest displacement crisis</td>\n      <td>12.0</td>\n      <td>-37.5</td>\n      <td>6</td>\n      <td>1.92</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>7</th>\n      <td>Gaza Conflict</td>\n      <td>2023</td>\n      <td>Active — fragile ceasefire</td>\n      <td>1.9</td>\n      <td>-40.5</td>\n      <td>5</td>\n      <td>0.23</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>8</th>\n      <td>Iran-Israel War</td>\n      <td>2025</td>\n      <td>Ceasefire (Jun 2025) — fragile</td>\n      <td>0.4</td>\n      <td>-5.0</td>\n      <td>7</td>\n      <td>0.56</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>9</th>\n      <td>Pakistan-Afghanistan War</td>\n      <td>2026</td>\n      <td>Active (Feb 27, 2026)</td>\n      <td>0.3</td>\n      <td>-3.5</td>\n      <td>4</td>\n      <td>0.34</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>10</th>\n      <td>Lebanon War (2026)</td>\n      <td>2026</td>\n      <td>Active — resumed Mar 2, 2026</td>\n      <td>0.5</td>\n      <td>-8.0</td>\n      <td>4</td>\n      <td>0.25</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n</div>"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":16},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# DATASET 2 — Monthly Economic Indicators (2018–2024)\n# Reflects real patterns from: World Bank, IMF, FAO, UNHCR\n\n# Create a monthly timeline from Jan 2018 to Dec 2024\ndates = pd.date_range(start='2018-01-01', end='2024-12-01', freq='MS')\nn = len(dates)\nnp.random.seed(42)  # makes results reproducible\n\n# Oil price (USD per barrel)\n# Real pattern: COVID crash 2020, Ukraine spike Feb 2022, then easing\noil_base   = np.linspace(65, 75, n) + np.random.normal(0, 3, n)\ncovid_dip  = np.where((dates >= '2020-03-01') & (dates <= '2020-06-01'),\n                      -40, 0)\nukraine_spike = np.where((dates >= '2022-02-01') & (dates <= '2022-08-01'),\n                          +45, 0)\nukraine_spike2 = np.where((dates >= '2022-08-01') & (dates <= '2023-06-01'),\n                           +15, 0)\noil_price  = np.clip(oil_base + covid_dip + ukraine_spike + ukraine_spike2, 15, 140)\n\n# Global food price index (FAO baseline = 100)\nfood_base  = np.linspace(95, 115, n) + np.random.normal(0, 2, n)\nfood_spike = np.where((dates >= '2022-02-01') & (dates <= '2022-05-01'),\n                       +45, 0)\nfood_ease  = np.where((dates >= '2022-05-01') & (dates <= '2023-12-01'),\n                       +15, 0)\nfood_index = food_base + food_spike + food_ease\n\n# Global inflation rate (%)\ninfl_base  = np.linspace(2.1, 2.8, n) + np.random.normal(0, 0.2, n)\ninfl_spike = np.where((dates >= '2021-09-01') & (dates <= '2023-06-01'),\n                       +5.5, 0)\ninfl_ease  = np.where((dates >= '2023-06-01') & (dates <= '2024-12-01'),\n                       +1.5, 0)\ninflation  = np.clip(infl_base + infl_spike + infl_ease, 0, 12)\n\n# Global refugee count (millions)\nrefugee_base  = np.linspace(25, 35, n)\nsyria_rise    = np.where(dates >= '2018-01-01', +8, 0)\nukraine_rise  = np.where(dates >= '2022-03-01', +10, 0)\nukraine_rise2 = np.where(dates >= '2022-06-01', +2,  0)\ngaza_rise     = np.where(dates >= '2023-10-01', +2,  0)\nrefugees      = refugee_base + syria_rise + ukraine_rise + ukraine_rise2 + gaza_rise\n\n# Combine into one DataFrame\necon = pd.DataFrame({\n    'date':        dates,\n    'oil_price':   np.round(oil_price,  2),\n    'food_index':  np.round(food_index, 1),\n    'inflation':   np.round(inflation,  2),\n    'refugees_M':  np.round(refugees,   1)\n})\necon.set_index('date', inplace=True)\n\nprint(\"Economic Indicators Dataset\")\nprint(f\"Shape: {econ.shape[0]} months × {econ.shape[1]} indicators\")\nprint(f\"Period: {econ.index[0].strftime('%b %Y')} → {econ.index[-1].strftime('%b %Y')}\")\nprint()\necon.head(8)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-03-20T19:19:58.550624Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-03-20T19:19:58.551031Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-03-20T19:19:58.594845Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-03-20T19:19:58.551003Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-03-20T19:19:58.593939Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Economic Indicators Dataset\nShape: 84 months × 4 indicators\nPeriod: Jan 2018 → Dec 2024\n\n","output_type":"stream"},{"execution_count":17,"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":"            oil_price  food_index  inflation  refugees_M\ndate                                                    \n2018-01-01      66.49        93.4       2.05        33.0\n2018-02-01      64.71        94.2       1.96        33.1\n2018-03-01      67.18        97.3       1.94        33.2\n2018-04-01      69.93        96.4       1.96        33.4\n2018-05-01      64.78        94.9       2.12        33.5\n2018-06-01      64.90        97.2       2.21        33.6\n2018-07-01      70.46        96.6       2.21        33.7\n2018-08-01      68.15        98.6       2.32        33.8","text/html":"<div>\n<style scoped>\n    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n        vertical-align: middle;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n        vertical-align: top;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe thead th {\n        text-align: right;\n    }\n</style>\n<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n      <th></th>\n    