lict events. The 2026 conflicts are especially important: Sudan has created the world's largest active displacement crisis (12M displaced, per IOM 2025), Myanmar's GDP fell 18% after the 2021 coup (UNDP), and new Middle East escalations in 2026 are already sending fresh shockwaves through oil markets and shipping lanes. The patterns reflect documented data from ACLED, UN OCHA, the African Development Bank, IMF, and UNHCR.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"---\n## 3 - Data Preprocessing\n\nRaw data is rarely ready to use. We need to clean it, add useful columns, and prepare it for charts and AI analysis.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# 1. Check for missing values\nprint(\"Missing values in economic data:\")\nprint(econ.isnull().sum())\nprint()\nprint(\"Missing values in conflict data:\")\nprint(conflicts.isnull().sum())\n\n# 2. Add useful derived columns to economic data\necon['year']           = econ.index.year\necon['month']          = econ.index.month\necon['oil_pct_change'] = econ['oil_price'].pct_change() * 100  # month-over-month % change\necon['ukraine_period'] = econ.index >= '2022-02-01'            # flag: before vs after war\n\n# 3. Print summary statistics\nprint(\"\\n Key Statistics\")\nprint(f\"Oil price range : ${econ['oil_price'].min():.0f} – ${econ['oil_price'].max():.0f} per barrel\")\nprint(f\"Max inflation   : {econ['inflation'].max():.1f}%\")\nprint(f\"Max refugees    : {econ['refugees_M'].max():.1f} million people\")\nprint(f\"Highest severity: {conflicts.loc[conflicts['severity_score'].idxmax(), 'conflict']}\")\nprint(f\"Total displaced : {conflicts['displaced_M'].sum():.1f} million across all conflicts\")\n\n# 4. Create pre/post Ukraine war comparison\npre_war  = econ[econ.index <  '2022-02-01'][['oil_price','food_index','inflation']].mean()\npost_war = econ[econ.index >= '2022-02-01'][['oil_price','food_index','inflation']].mean()\n\ncomparison = pd.DataFrame({'Before Ukraine War': pre_war, 'After Ukraine War': post_war})\ncomparison['Change %'] = ((post_war - pre_war) / pre_war * 100).round(1).astype(str) + '%'\nprint(\"\\n Ukraine War Impact: Before vs After\")\nprint(comparison.round(2))\n\n# 5. Show top 5 conflicts by severity score\nprint(\"\\n Top 5 Conflicts by Global Ripple Severity\")\nprint(conflicts[['conflict','start_year','severity_score']]\n      .sort_values('severity_score', ascending=False)\n      .head(5)\n      .to_string(index=False))","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-03-20T19:19:58.596489Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-03-20T19:19:58.596898Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-03-20T19:19:58.628400Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-03-20T19:19:58.596838Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-03-20T19:19:58.627227Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Missing values in economic data:\noil_price     0\nfood_index    0\ninflation     0\nrefugees_M    0\ndtype: int64\n\nMissing values in conflict data:\nconflict              0\ncountry               0\nstart_year            0\nstatus_2026           0\nregion                0\nintensity             0\ndisplaced_M           0\ngdp_shock_pct         0\nneighbors_affected    0\nseverity_score        0\ndtype: int64\n\n Key Statistics\nOil price range : $25 – $134 per barrel\nMax inflation   : 9.5%\nMax refugees    : 57.0 million people\nHighest severity: Syria Civil War\nTotal displaced : 49.8 million across all conflicts\n\n Ukraine War Impact: Before vs After\n            Before Ukraine War  After Ukraine War Change %\noil_price                64.04              86.73    35.4%\nfood_index              100.68             124.89    24.0%\ninflation                 2.89               6.13   111.8%\n\n Top 5 Conflicts by Global Ripple Severity\n         conflict  start_year  severity_score\n  Syria Civil War        2011            3.62\n         Iraq War        2003            2.47\n      Ukraine War        2022            2.25\n  Sudan Civil War        2023            1.92\nMyanmar Civil War        2021            0.83\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":18},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**What this cell does:**  \nCleans both datasets, checks for missing values, adds useful new columns (like year, month, and month-over-month oil price change), and creates a before/after comparison for the Ukraine war.\n\n**Why:** Raw data is like uncooked ingredients - you can't serve it directly. We're adding columns that make patterns easier to spot (like flagging which months occurred after the Ukraine invasion). The conflict dataset already includes a `severity_score` column - a simple formula that ranks conflicts by their global ripple effect, not just their local damage. Sudan scores very high because 12M people were displaced and 6 neighboring countries were affected, even though it gets far less news coverage than Ukraine.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"---\n## 4 - Visualization\n\nThree charts, each telling one part of the butterfly effect story.  \nEvery spike you see in these charts corresponds to a real conflict event.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# CHART 1 — Oil Price Timeline with War Annotations\n# Story: Watch how conflict events cause immediate oil price shocks\n\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(14, 5))\n\n# Main line\nax.plot(econ.index, econ['oil_price'], color='#f0a500', linewidth=2, zorder=3)\nax.fill_between(econ.index, econ['oil_price'], alpha=0.15, color='#f0a500')\n\n# Shade the Ukraine war period\nax.axvspan(pd.Timestamp('2022-02-01'), pd.Timestamp('2022-08-01'),\n           alpha=0.15, color='#ff4444', label='Ukraine War spike')\nax.axvspan(pd.Timestamp('2020-03-01'), pd.Timestamp('2020-06-01'),\n           alpha=0.15, color='#4444ff', label='COVID-19 crash')\n\n# Annotation arrows\nax.annotate('COVID-19\\nDemand Crash', xy=(pd.Timestamp('2020-04-01'), 20),\n            xytext=(pd.Timestamp('2019-06-01'), 10),\n            fontsize=9, color='#aaaaff',\n            arrowprops=dict(arrowstyle='->', color='#aaaaff', lw=1.5))\nax.annotate('Russia invades\\nUkraine', xy=(pd.Timestamp('2022-06-01'), 115),\n            xytext=(pd.Timestamp('2023-01-01'), 125),\n            fontsize=9, color='#ff8888',\n            arrowprops=dict(arrowstyle='->', color='#ff8888', lw=1.5))\n\nax.set_title('  Global Oil Price (USD/barrel) — 2018 to 2024\\nHow wars send shockwaves through energy markets',\n             fontsize=13, pad=15)\nax.set_ylabel('Price (USD per barrel)')\nax.set_xlabel('Date')\nax.legend(loc='upper left', fontsize=9)\nax.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\nax.set_ylim(0, 145)\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.savefig('chart1_oil_prices.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\nplt.show()\nprint(\" Chart 1 saved.\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-03-20T19:19:58.629474Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-03-20T19:19:58.629741Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-03-20T19:19:59.403172Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-03-20T19:19:58.629719Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-03-20T19:19:59.402099Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1400x500 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"name":"stdout","text":" Chart 1 saved.\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":19},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# CHART 2 — Food Price Index & Inflation (dual axis)\n# Story: War in Ukraine + Russia disrupted 30% of global wheat supply\n\nfig, ax1 = plt.subplots(figsize=(14, 5))\nax2 = ax1.twinx()   # second y-axis on the right\n\n# Food price index (left axis)\nax1.plot(econ.index, econ['food_index'], color='#44cc88', linewidth=2, label='Food Price Index')\nax1.fill_between(econ.index, econ['food_index'], 90, alpha=0.1, color='#44cc88')\nax1.set_ylabel('FAO Food Price Index (100 = baseline)', color='#44cc88')\nax1.tick_params(axis='y', labelcolor='#44cc88')\n\n# Inflation (right axis)\nax2.plot(econ.index, econ['inflation'], color='#ff6688', linewidth=2,\n         linestyle='--', label='Global Inflation %')\nax2.set_ylabel('Inflation Rate (%)', color='#ff6688')\nax2.tick_params(axis='y', labelcolor='#ff6688')\n\n# Mark the Ukraine war start\nax1.axvline(pd.Timestamp('2022-02-24'), color='red', linestyle=':', linewidth=2, alpha=0.7)\nax1.text(pd.Timestamp('2022-03-15'), 100, 'Ukraine\\nInvasion\\nFeb 24, 2022',\n         fontsize=8, color='#ff8888')\n\n# Legend\nlines1, labels1 = ax1.get_legend_handles_labels()\nlines2, labels2 = ax2.get_legend_handles_labels()\nax1.legend(lines1 + lines2, labels1 + labels2, loc='upper left', fontsize=9)\n\nax1.set_title('  Food Prices vs Global Inflation — The Wheat Butterfly Effect\\n'\n              'Ukraine + Russia = 30% of world wheat exports. When they stopped, everyone felt it.',\n              fontsize=12, pad=15)\nax1.set_xlabel('Date')\nax1.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.savefig('chart2_food_inflation.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\nplt.show()\nprint(\" Chart 2 saved.\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-03-20T19:19:59.404779Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-03-20T19:19:59.405151Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-03-20T19:20:00.328183Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-03-20T19:19:59.405124Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-03-20T19:20:00.326955Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1400x500 with 2 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"name":"stdout","text":" Chart 2 saved.\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":20},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# CHART 3 - Global Refugee Crisis Timeline + Conflict Severity Heatmap\n# Story: Each conflict wave added millions more displaced people\n\nfig, (ax1, ax2) = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(16, 5))\n\n# Left: Refugee timeline\nax1.fill_between(econ.index, econ['refugees_M'], alpha=0.4, color='#aa88ff')\nax1.plot(econ.index, econ['refugees_M'], color='#aa88ff', linewidth=2)\n\n# Annotate each wave\nwaves = [\n    ('2018-06-01', 35, 'Pre-existing\\nSyria refugees'),\n    ('2022-06-01', 52, 'Ukraine\\n+8M refugees'),\n    ('2023-12-01', 60, 'Gaza\\n+2M displaced'),\n]\nfor date, y, label in waves:\n    ax1.annotate(label, xy=(pd.Timestamp(date), y),\n                 fontsize=8, color='#ccaaff', ha='center')\n\nax1.set_title('  Global Refugees & Displaced People (Millions)\\nEach conflict adds a new wave', fontsize=11)\nax1.set_ylabel('People displaced (millions)')\nax1.set_xlabel('Date')\nax1.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n\n# Right: Conflict severity heatmap\nheat_data = conflicts.set_index('conflict')[['displaced_M', 'neighbors_affected',\n                                             'gdp_shock_pct', 'severity_score']].copy()\nheat_data['gdp_shock_pct'] = heat_data['gdp_shock_pct'].abs()  # make positive for color\nheat_norm = (heat_data - heat_data.min()) / (heat_data.max() - heat_data.min())  # normalize 0-1\n\nsns.heatmap(heat_norm, ax=ax2,\n            cmap='RdYlGn_r',   # red = high impact\n            linewidths=0.5,\n            annot=heat_data.round(1),  # show real numbers, not normalized\n            fmt='g',\n            cbar_kws={'label': 'Relative Impact (0=low, 1=high)'})\n\nax2.set_title('  Conflict Impact Heatmap\\nDarker red = bigger ripple effect on the world', fontsize=11)\nax2.set_xticklabels(['Displaced\\n(M)', 'Neighbors\\nAffected', 'GDP\\nShock %', 'Severity\\nScore'],\n                    rotation=0, fontsize=9)\nax2.set_yticklabels(ax2.get_yticklabels(), rotation=0, fontsize=8)\n\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.savefig('chart3_refugees_heatmap.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\nplt.show()\nprint(\" Chart 3 saved.\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-03-20T19:20:00.329414Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-03-20T19:20:00.329799Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-03-20T19:20:01.658221Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-03-20T19:20:00.329692Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-03-20T19:20:01.656259Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1600x500 with 3 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"name":"stdout","text":" Chart 3 saved.\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":21},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**What these cells do:**  \nBuild three charts, each telling a different part of the war butterfly effect story:\n1. **Oil prices** - shows the energy shockwave from Ukraine (price nearly doubled in months)\n2. **Food prices + inflation** - shows how blocking Ukrainian wheat ports caused global hunger and inflation together\n3. **Refugee waves + heatmap** - shows the human cost accumulating over years, and which conflicts had the biggest global ripple\n\n**Why:** A number in a table doesn't tell a story. A chart with an annotation that says \"Russia invades Ukraine\" right where the price spikes — that tells a story instantly. Recruiters and Kaggle voters respond to visuals that make the data obvious.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"---\n## 5 - Gemma 3 Model Integration\n\nNow we load the actual AI brain - Gemma 3 (4B instruction-tuned).  \nWe use `bfloat16` precision (half the memory of normal) and `device_map=\"auto\"` so it automatically uses the GPU.\n\n**Memory note:** The 4B model uses ~8GB of VRAM. Kaggle's T4 GPU has 15GB — we have a comfortable buffer.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# LOAD GEMMA 3 — The AI brain of this project\n\n# Path where Kaggle stored the model files we added earlier\nMODEL_PATH = \"/kaggle/input/models/google/gemma-3/transformers/gemma-3-4b-it/1\"\n\nprint(\"Step 1/2: Loading tokenizer (the word-to-number converter)...\")\ntokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(MODEL_PATH)\nprint(\"Tokenizer loaded\")\n\nprint(\"\\nStep 2/2: Loading Gemma 3 model onto GPU...\")\nprint(\"   (This takes 1–3 minutes - the model is ~8GB)\")\n\nmodel = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(\n    MODEL_PATH,\n    torch_dtype=torch.bfloat16,   # half precision = half memory usage\n    device_map=\"auto\"             # auto-detects and uses GPU\n)\nmodel.eval()  # set to evaluation mode (not training mode)\n\n# Report memory usage\nif device == 'cuda':\n    used_mem = torch.cuda.memory_allocated() / 1e9\n    total_mem = torch.cuda.get_device_properties(0).total_memory / 1e9\n    print(f\"\\n Model loaded successfully!\")\n    print(f\"   GPU memory used : {used_mem:.1f} GB / {total_mem:.1f} GB\")\n    print(f\"   Memory remaining: {total_mem - used_mem:.1f} GB free\")\nelse:\n    print(\"\\n Model loaded (CPU mode - will be slower)\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-03-20T19:20:01.659591Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-03-20T19:20:01.660264Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-03-20T19:20:08.540457Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-03-20T19:20:01.660222Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-03-20T19:20:08.533383Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Step 1/2: Loading tokenizer (the word-to-number converter)...\nTokenizer loaded\n\nStep 2/2: Loading Gemma 3 model onto GPU...\n   (This takes 1–3 minutes - the model is ~8GB)\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"Loading weights:   0%|          | 0/883 [00:00<?, ?it/s]","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_minor":0,"model_id":"4d6c4ef1b73748bc8032faff8de4346c"}},"metadata":{}},{"name":"stdout","text":"\n Model loaded (CPU mode - will be slower)\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":22},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**What this cell does:**  \nLoads two things from the model files: the **tokenizer** (converts your English text into numbers the AI understands) and the **model itself** (the actual intelligence that generates responses).\n\n**Why `bfloat16`?** By default, AI models store their numbers in full 32-bit precision — very accurate but very memory-hungry. `bfloat16` cuts that in half with almost no loss in quality. Think of it like compressing a photo from RAW to JPEG — still looks great, takes half the space.\n\n**Why `device_map=\"auto\"`?** This tells Transformers to automatically figure out how to spread the model across available hardware (GPU + CPU if needed). You don't have to manually manage any of that.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"---\n## 6 - The Cause - Effect Chain Generator\n\nThis is the heart of the project.  \n\nWe build a function that takes any conflict event as plain English input and asks Gemma 3 to trace the full butterfly effect — from the war itself, all the way to real-world consequences in other countries.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# THE BUTTERFLY EFFECT CHAIN GENERATOR\n# Input : a conflict event (plain English)\n# Output: a structured cause → effect chain (AI-generated)\n\ndef generate_butterfly_chain(conflict_event: str,\n                              max_tokens: int = 400) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Takes a war/conflict event and returns a structured\n    cause-and-effect chain showing its global ripple effects.\n\n    Args:\n        conflict_event: Plain English description of a conflict\n                        e.g. \"Russia invades Ukraine in February 2022\"\n        max_tokens    : Maximum length of the AI response\n\n    Returns:\n        A formatted string showing the butterfly effect chain\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Build the prompt\n    # We give Gemma 3 clear, structured instructions\n    # The more specific we are, the better the output\n    prompt_text = f\"\"\"You are an expert geopolitical economist who specializes in analyzing \\\nhow wars and conflicts create ripple effects across the global economy and society.\n\nAnalyze this conflict event: \"{conflict_event}\"\n\nTrace the complete butterfly effect — show how this single event triggers a chain of \\\nconsequences across energy, food, trade, migration, and politics in other countries.\n\nFormat your response EXACTLY like this:\n\nTRIGGER: [The conflict event]\n\nCHAIN REACTION:\n1. [Immediate effect — within days/weeks]\n2. [Short-term ripple — within months]\n3. [Medium-term ripple — within 6-12 months]\n4. [Long-term ripple — 1-3 years later]\n5. [Global systemic effect]\n\nCOUNTRIES MOST AFFECTED: [List 3-5 specific countries and why]\n\nKEY NUMBERS: [Include 2-3 real statistics that show the scale]\n\nHIDDEN RIPPLE: [One surprising or non-obvious consequence most people miss]\n\"\"\"\n\n    # Format for Gemma 3's chat template\n    messages = [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": prompt_text}]\n    formatted = tokenizer.apply_chat_template(\n        messages,\n        tokenize=False,\n        add_generation_prompt=True\n    )\n\n    # Tokenize (convert text → numbers)\n    inputs = tokenizer(\n        formatted,\n        return_tensors=\"pt\",\n        truncation=True,\n        max_length=1024\n    ).to(model.device)\n\n    # Generate the response\n    with torch.no_grad():   # don't track gradients — saves memory\n        output_ids = model.generate(\n            **inputs,\n            max_new_tokens=max_tokens,\n            do_sample=True,\n            temperature=0.7,     # 0 = robotic, 1 = creative. 0.7 = balanced\n            top_p=0.9,           # only consider top 90% probability words\n            repetition_penalty=1.1,  # discourage repeating phrases\n            pad_token_id=tokenizer.eos_token_id\n        )\n\n    # Decode (convert numbers → text)\n    full_text = tokenizer.decode(output_ids[0], skip_special_tokens=True)\n\n    # Extract only the model's answer (remove the question we sent)\n    if 'model' in full_text.lower():\n        # Split on 'model' marker that Gemma uses to signal its reply\n        parts = full_text.split('model')\n        response = parts[-1].strip()\n    else:\n        response = full_text.strip()\n\n    return response\n\n\nprint(\"Butterfly Chain Generator is ready.\")\nprint(\"   Call: generate_butterfly_chain('your conflict event here')\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-03-20T19:20:08.545421Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-03-20T19:20:08.545836Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-03-20T19:20:08.576063Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-03-20T19:20:08.545798Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-03-20T19:20:08.561706Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Butterfly Chain Generator is ready.\n   Call: generate_butterfly_chain('your conflict event here')\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":23},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**What this cell does:**  \nDefines the main function of this entire project - `generate_butterfly_chain()`. It takes any conflict event as input, builds a carefully structured prompt, sends it to Gemma 3, and returns a formatted cause-effect chain.\n\n**Why does the prompt structure matter?** Giving the AI a clear template (\"Format your response EXACTLY like this\") dramatically improves output quality. Without structure, the AI might give a rambling essay. With structure, it gives numbered steps, affected countries, and key statistics - exactly what we need.\n\n**Why `torch.no_grad()`?** By default, PyTorch tracks every calculation in case we want to train the model. We're not training - we're just asking questions. Turning off gradient tracking cuts memory usage by roughly 40%.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"---\n## 7 - Sample AI Outputs\n\nLet's run the generator on three real conflicts and see the butterfly chains Gemma 3 produces.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# EXAMPLE 1 - Ukraine 2022\n# The most economically disruptive conflict of the last decade\n\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\nprint(\"BUTTERFLY EFFECT ANALYSIS — EXAMPLE 1\")\nprint(\"=\" * 65)\n\nevent_1 = \"Russia invades Ukraine on February 24, 2022\"\nprint(f\"\\n Input: {event_1}\\n\")\nprint(\"-\" * 65)\n\nresult_1 = generate_butterfly_chain(event_1)\nprint(result_1)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-03-20T19:20:08.577608Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-03-20T19:20:08.578180Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-03-20T19:26:09.649809Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-03-20T19:20:08.578145Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-03-20T19:26:09.648526Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"